# React Patterns

## Components
- Use `function`, not `const`, for component definitions
- One component per file; named export only
- Props via destructured object where it improves readability
- No `-er` suffix in component names (no Managers, Controllers, Handlers)

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD
export function ClayCard({ title, children, variant = 'default' }) { ... }

// ❌ BAD
const ClayCard = (props) => { ... }
export default ClayCard
```

## Component Boundaries

- Prefer presentational components that receive data via props
- Keep domain decisions and normalization in `src/lib/**` when they are reused or test-sensitive
- Use hooks and effects only in interactive components that truly need them
- Avoid turning static Astro-rendered sections into client components without a clear reason
- Keep functions short — no blank lines inside function bodies

## Claymorphism Design System
The project uses a custom clay design system. Use these CSS classes from `src/styles/global.css`:

```
clay-card          - white card with clay shadow
clay-card-mint     - teal/mint colored card
clay-card-peach    - peach colored card
clay-card-blue     - blue colored card
clay-card-lavender - lavender colored card
clay-card-soft-*   - pastel pale versions (soft-mint, soft-peach, soft-blue, soft-lavender)
btn-clay-primary   - primary teal pill button
btn-clay-secondary - white secondary pill button
btn-clay-white     - white button
icon-circle-*      - colored icon circle (mint, peach, blue, lavender, yellow)
blob-mint/peach/blue/lavender - organic background blob shapes
num-badge          - numbered step badge
stat-pill          - small stat label
avatar-ring-*      - colored ring around avatar (peach, blue, mint, lavender)
```

Never use `box-shadow` inline when a clay utility class exists.

## Static Content
- Keep static arrays and strings **outside** the component function
- Use a `const` named in UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for static data arrays

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD
const NAV_ITEMS = [{ label: 'Маммология', to: '/mammology' }]

export function Nav() {
  return NAV_ITEMS.map(item => <NavLink key={item.to} {...item} />)
}
```

## Styling

- Prefer Tailwind utilities and shared clay classes over ad-hoc inline styles
- When a visual pattern repeats, add or reuse a named utility in `src/styles/global.css`
- Keep class composition readable; extract repeated class strings when necessary
- Never use pure black text — use `clay-dark` or `clay-text` tokens

## Performance

- Minimize client-side state and hydration
- Always add `loading="lazy"` to non-critical `<img>` tags
- Prefer modern compressed assets (WebP) and always specify meaningful `alt`, `width`, and `height`
- Avoid expensive effects that can be replaced by CSS or Astro-rendered markup
- Use the lightest viable Astro client directive (`client:idle` > `client:load` when appropriate)

## Responsive
- Mobile-first with Tailwind breakpoints: `sm:` `md:` `lg:`
- Default layout is single column; expand with `sm:grid-cols-2`, `lg:grid-cols-4`

## Accessibility

- Use semantic elements before adding ARIA
- Ensure interactive controls have accessible names
- Keep keyboard interaction intact for menus, dialogs, and forms
- Do not rely on color alone to communicate state
- Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for body text (WCAG AA)
- Touch targets: minimum 44px for mobile
- Icons: Lucide React only, never emojis
